<div class="reveal">
  <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.28em] uppercase text-indigo-300/80 mb-5">§02 · Quickstart</p>
  <h1 class="font-display text-[42px] md:text-[62px] leading-[1.0] tracking-[-0.025em] text-white font-light">
    From source to a
    <span class="font-display italic text-indigo-200/90 font-light">working broker</span>
    in one command.
  </h1>
</div>

<p class="reveal d1 mt-7 text-[17px] leading-[1.7] text-slate-300 max-w-[58ch] font-light">
  The demo script builds the workspace, boots the broker with a deliberately tiny segment size so log rolls are visible, produces 200&nbsp;records into a two-partition topic, consumes through a consumer group, restarts the broker mid-stream, and verifies that the offsets survived.
</p>

<div class="reveal d2 mt-8 codeblock">
  <div class="codeblock-bar">
    <span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span>
    <span class="label">bash</span>
    <span class="lang">one-shot</span>
  </div>
<pre><span class="c-fn">$</span> make demo</pre>
</div>

<p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 -mt-3 mb-2"><em>Equivalent to <code>bash scripts/demo.sh</code>.</em> The script ends with <code class="text-emerald-300">DEMO OK</code> on success.</p>

<div class="rule-x my-14"></div>

<h2><span class="num">§</span>Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Rust 1.75+</strong> (this project is developed on 1.95).</li>
  <li>A free TCP port — default <code>127.0.0.1:9876</code>; override with <code>ES_PORT</code>.</li>
  <li>Optional: <code>curl</code> if you want to poke the API by hand.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="num">§</span>What the script actually does</h2>
<div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
  <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
    <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-white/[0.05] ring-1 ring-white/[0.1] flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-[11px] text-indigo-200">01</span>
    <div>
      <p class="font-display text-[17px] text-white tracking-tight">Reset</p>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-slate-400">Wipes <code>./data</code> so the run is reproducible.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
    <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-white/[0.05] ring-1 ring-white/[0.1] flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-[11px] text-indigo-200">02</span>
    <div>
      <p class="font-display text-[17px] text-white tracking-tight">Build</p>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-slate-400">Compiles the workspace in release mode.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
    <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-white/[0.05] ring-1 ring-white/[0.1] flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-[11px] text-indigo-200">03</span>
    <div>
      <p class="font-display text-[17px] text-white tracking-tight">Boot the broker</p>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-slate-400">Starts <code>es-broker</code> in the background with <code>--segment-bytes 1024</code>, then polls <code>/healthz</code> until it's ready.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
    <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-white/[0.05] ring-1 ring-white/[0.1] flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-[11px] text-indigo-200">04</span>
    <div>
      <p class="font-display text-[17px] text-white tracking-tight">Produce 200 records</p>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-slate-400">Creates topic <code>orders</code> with two partitions, then writes <code>v0…v199</code>. The tiny segment size guarantees multiple log rolls per partition.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
    <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-white/[0.05] ring-1 ring-white/[0.1] flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-[11px] text-indigo-200">05</span>
    <div>
      <p class="font-display text-[17px] text-white tracking-tight">Consume + commit + restart</p>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-slate-400">Reads 5 records as group <code>analytics</code>, commits offset 5, kills the broker, restarts it, confirms the offset survived, then resumes from 5.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2><span class="num">§</span>Driving it manually</h2>
<p>Two terminals — broker on one side, CLI on the other:</p>

<div class="codeblock">
  <div class="codeblock-bar">
    <span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span>
    <span class="label">terminal 1</span>
    <span class="lang">broker</span>
  </div>
<pre><span class="c-fn">$</span> cargo build <span class="c-key">--release</span>
<span class="c-fn">$</span> ./target/release/es-broker <span class="c-key">\</span>
    <span class="c-key">--data-dir</span> ./data <span class="c-key">\</span>
    <span class="c-key">--bind</span> <span class="c-str">127.0.0.1:9876</span> <span class="c-key">\</span>
    <span class="c-key">--segment-bytes</span> <span class="c-num">1024</span></pre>
</div>

<div class="codeblock">
  <div class="codeblock-bar">
    <span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span>
    <span class="label">terminal 2</span>
    <span class="lang">cli</span>
  </div>
<pre><span class="c-fn">$</span> <span class="c-key">export</span> ES_BROKER=<span class="c-str">http://127.0.0.1:9876</span>
<span class="c-fn">$</span> es topic create <span class="c-key">--name</span> orders <span class="c-key">--partitions</span> <span class="c-num">2</span>
<span class="c-fn">$</span> es produce <span class="c-key">--topic</span> orders <span class="c-key">--key</span> k1 <span class="c-key">--value</span> <span class="c-str">'{"id":1}'</span>
<span class="c-fn">$</span> es consume <span class="c-key">--topic</span> orders <span class="c-key">--partition</span> <span class="c-num">0</span> <span class="c-key">--offset</span> <span class="c-num">0</span></pre>
</div>

<h2><span class="num">§</span>The test suite</h2>
<p>
  The in-process integration tests at <code>crates/es-broker/tests/end_to_end.rs</code> spawn the broker on an ephemeral port (<code>127.0.0.1:0</code>) and drive it via <code>reqwest</code>. They cover segment rolls, group resume, restart-persistence, torn-write recovery, and stable key routing.
</p>

<div class="codeblock">
  <div class="codeblock-bar">
    <span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span>
    <span class="label">tests</span>
    <span class="lang">cargo</span>
  </div>
<pre><span class="c-fn">$</span> cargo test <span class="c-key">--workspace</span>
<span class="c-com">test storage::record::tests::roundtrip_with_key       ...</span> <span class="c-add">ok</span>
<span class="c-com">test storage::record::tests::detects_corruption       ...</span> <span class="c-add">ok</span>
<span class="c-com">test produce_then_consume_with_segment_rolls          ...</span> <span class="c-add">ok</span>
<span class="c-com">test group_resume_and_restart_persistence             ...</span> <span class="c-add">ok</span>
<span class="c-com">test recovers_from_torn_write                         ...</span> <span class="c-add">ok</span>
<span class="c-com">test key_routing_is_stable                            ...</span> <span class="c-add">ok</span>

<span class="c-em">test result:</span> <span class="c-add">ok.</span> 11 passed; 0 failed</pre>
</div>
